The interaction parameter of water with the polymer blend was then calculated using Eq. (4) (Table 4). Taking the swelling of the polymer blends into account demonstrated that equilibrium swelling ratio increased, decreased, and again increased with the change in PG content from 6 to 30 wt. %, from 30 to 45 wt. %, and from 45 to 60 wt. %, respectively (Fig. 6). The trend of change in the equilibrium swelling ratio of the blends was in accordance with the variations in the interaction parameter of the solvent (water) and the polymer blend (

                              χ

